     <h1 class="title" title="Nandi Hills">Nandi Hills</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/Nandi-hills.jpg" title="Nandi Hills" alt="Nandi Hills, hill stations in india, South india hill stations" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


The 1,478 m high Nandi Hills, <b>Karnataka</b> is the source of many rivers. Nearby hills and forests full of wildlife. Around the Nandi Hills are several small hills that can be visited on foot. Nandi Hills has a temperate climate all year round. Nandi Hills or Nandi Hills is named after the <b>bull of Lord Shiva. Pleasant Hill station</b>, Nandi Hills is also known as <b>Nandigiri</b>  or <b>Nandidurga</b> among occupants. The Nandi Hills have attracted people since long. Nandi Hills has been the haunt of <b>Tipu Sultan</b> and the British. Tipu Sultan's palace and bungalows of the British position in his testimony before the same.</p>





